  "goodToKnow": "Der Oberbürgermeister (die Oberbürgermeisterin), often just der OB, is the mayor of a larger city, while small towns have a Bürgermeister. In most German states, mayors are directly elected by the people. In Berlin, Hamburg and Bremen, which are also states, the head is called der Regierende or Erste Bürgermeister. A word with 17 letters and five syllables, typical of German titles."
